 "notes": "CAPP-12T multi-cell cavity haloscope. 90% CL exclusion digitised from Fig. 5 (e-print raster Sensitivity.png, 12000x3000 px) which plots g_agamma/g_KSVZ vs mass over 21.86-22.00 ueV; axis calibration from tick marks, dashed line at ratio=1.00 confirmed. Ratio converted to g_agamma using g_KSVZ(m) = (alpha/2pi)*1.92/f_a with m_a = 5.7 ueV x (10^12 GeV/f_a), i.e. g_KSVZ = 3.91e-16 GeV^-1 x m[ueV]. Mean extracted ratio 0.932 matches the paper's quoted limit g >~ 0.93 g_KSVZ. Paper assumes rho_a = 0.45 GeV/cm^3 (canonical, no rescaling). Small gap near 21.907 ueV where the curve goes off-scale due to TE313 mode mixing (21.90-21.92 ueV); flanks of that spike and the off-scale rises at both mass edges are included as traced (capped at plot top, ratio ~2.19). 110 points binned from ~8200 pixel columns.",
